      section: "3.2",
      title: "Correction of errors",
      summary: "Errors are corrected with journal entries that remove the wrong effect and put in the right one. Errors that upset the agreement of the trial balance are corrected through a suspense account, which must end with a nil balance. Some errors change the profit for the year and the figures in the statement of financial position, so a statement of corrected profit is often needed.",
